      },
      {
        q: "Can I bring fruit through TSA — bananas, grapes, oranges?",
        a: "Yes, fresh fruits are allowed through TSA security in carry-on and checked bags for domestic US flights. On international routes, customs agencies may restrict bringing fruits across borders — for example, oranges and fresh fruits into Canada or Australia may be confiscated at customs. Always check destination country rules before packing fruit in your checked bag for an international trip."
      },
      {
        q: "Can I bring yogurt, peanut butter, honey, jam, and jelly through TSA?",
